      "technical_explanation": "The signal fires on URL-like literals, and the visible occurrences are all disclosed, purpose-matching network flows: relative same-origin calls to the host SillyTavern server for saving generated media and proxying one image provider, authenticated with the host context request headers; fetches of the extension's own stored image paths for cropping and download previews; base64 conversion and compression of reference and generated images before they are sent; and calls to the image-generation providers the user configures. These destinations and the sending of prompts and reference photos to the configured provider, including the third-party provider, are described openly in the project documentation as the extension's core purpose. No hardcoded, undisclosed, or off-purpose external destination is shown in the supplied windows.",
